            { text = "Members of the Dreamgrove discord developed this cooldown planner tool including the many CDR options in the Balance Druid tree. This tool can be pretty handy if you are interested in seeing how they interact with each other or want to plan cooldowns for an upcoming boss.", spellId = nil },
            { text = "You can hold a charge of at any time to better line up with a mechanic as long as you are not sitting on 2 charges.", spellId = 194223 },
            { text = "Remember that for Keeper of the Grove, the talent lets you hold any use of , / and for up to 15 seconds and will reduce the cooldown depending on how long it was held. This opens up for flexibility in your cooldown windows, where you can hold on to the ability in order to use it for specific mechanics in a fight.", spellId = 434249 },
            { text = "Have an idea of what is going to happen later in the fight. Be aware of what mechanics are coming, and then make a decision about your positioning and how much Astral Power you need to have available if you get targeted by a mechanic. You can also use instant casts like during your animation!", spellId = 78674 },
            { text = "can be a really good tool to help you with movement, and some fights can allow you to hold on to a charge of Eclipse if it means you can maintain full uptime during the mechanic, by using the instant casts from . Keep in mind that you still have to pool resources for the Eclipse windows!", spellId = 1239669 },
            { text = "Recognize and take advantage of situations where you can plant and cast or . These moments are valuable, and you want to avoid micro moving too much and getting gaps in your casts!", spellId = 194153 },
            { text = "If you want to get an easy view of your casting uptime, the Timeline feature on the WoWAnalyzer website is pretty good. If you have a log of your character from Warcraftlogs then you can paste the link into the website and navigate to your character. You will get a warning that the spec is not supported, but if you are only using the Timeline feature you can ignore this warning. There are a few other useful tidbits on here, like a count of how much Astral Power you wasted during the encounter and how active you were during your cooldown windows.", spellId = nil },
        },
